            <div xml:id="d764">

                <pb facs="1012" n="898" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg898"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.114 I’m Alone/2185: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Montreal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Frost</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-05-18T18:00:00-04:00">May 18, 1931—6
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Referring your inquiry by telephone concerning subpoenas served on you and on
                    Doris Corrigan requiring testimony concerning official acts and production
                    official documents at habeas corpus hearing of Marvin J. Clark.</p>
                <p>Advise appropriate authorities that under principles of international law
                    official archives of consular offices are not subject to subpoena requiring
                    production in judicial proceedings and that consular officers and their
                    employees cannot properly be required to testify concerning their official acts.
                    Add that accordingly you have been instructed by your Government not to appear
                    nor to permit Miss Corrigan to appear or produce records in response to the
                    subpoena.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Castle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
